# Opus Quad fixture: opus-lighting-hello-prefix
# Quoted bytes, not a full capture: the first 0x24 bytes of the type-0x10
# packet an Opus Quad sends to port 50002 of a device that announced itself
# as rekordbox, as matched by
#   https://github.com/kyleawayan/opus-quad-pro-dj-link-analysis/blob/main/pro-dj-link.js
#     (array `firstPacketOn50002FromOpusQuad`)
# The rest of the packet is not published; this prefix is what the
# analysis script compares to recognise the unit.
# Documented in: docs/protocols/opus-quad.md#what-the-unit-sends
# Name "OPUS-QUAD", byte 0x21 = 0x09 (where status packets carry the device
# number; its meaning in this packet is not published).
# Bytes: UDP payload, hex, 16 per line.
51 73 70 74 31 57 6d 4a 4f 4c 10 4f 50 55 53 2d
51 55 41 44 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 01
00 09 00 00
